Where a data.js node test goes (task 5834 split, 2026-10-14). The old 3,149-line dashboard/tests/js/data_poll.test.mjs is now five per-feature suites:
- data_poll: the poll loop (contract and auto-start, startPolling, in-flight guard, per-attempt deadline, backoff, jitter, df-data-refresh dispatch, 'Slowness pacing');
- data_apply: endpointsFor registry, applyKey, datumFor, keep-prior on failure;
- data_freshness: DF_DATA.__stale/__receipt publication;
- data_on_demand: ON_DEMAND_KEYS/requestOnDemand, REFRESH_OUTCOMES, onDemandView/onDemandDatum;
- data_scope: pollSetFor/scopePollingToTab and the rail badges.
Every suite loads data.js only through _data_loader.mjs::loadDataJs, which returns {api, window, events, fetchCalls, intervalCalls}; never copy it. Literals and stubs shared across suites (EXPECTED_ENDPOINT_COUNT, PLAIN_SPEC/DATUM_SPEC, CURATOR/COSTS/TASKS_PATH, TERMINAL_PROJECT, STALE_FAILURE_THRESHOLD, okResponse) live in _data_fixtures.mjs. Single-suite helpers stay in their suite.

