Completed: Make the backend one descriptor and the serve composition testable (cli.py::_serve)
Description: Two findings at one function. (1) The backend axis is decided in three places in cli.py: the _model match, the banner choice ('' only for api) and the operator-password requirement (api only); a fourth backend-dependent behaviour would be a fourth inline check (docs/code-quality.md heuristic 3, one mechanism per axis of variability). (2) _serve is the composition root (Host allow-list including INTAKE_PUBLIC_URL's netloc, notice versus disclaimer wiring, banner, password gate) and has no test because it ends in serve_forever; a wiring mistake there, such as swapping the notice and disclaimer arguments, would pass the suite. Only this run's smoke walk exercised it (lens tests).
Analysis: Premises verified on task/9 at 368e171 (the branch_base_sha; tree clean; baseline `uv run pytest` in this worktree: 31 passed). src/scoping_intake/cli.py decides the backend axis three times: _model (a match on the backend string), the banner (`"" if arguments.backend == "api" else PLAY_BANNER`) and the start check (`arguments.backend == "api" and not operator_password`). This is finding fk-64b288036fdf (heuristic 3). _serve is the composition root. It builds the Intake (SessionStore, model, CalibrationLog on INTAKE_DATA_DIR) and two Site values: the prospect site's hosts are the loopback names of --prospect-port plus INTAKE_PUBLIC_URL's netloc; the operator site's hosts are the loopback names of --operator-port, with its password from INTAKE_OPERATOR_PASSWORD. It then binds both and calls serve_forever, so none of this wiring is tested (finding fk-02c1a68a55f9). prospect_routes(intake, notice, disclaimer, banner) and operator_routes(intake, public_url, disclaimer) take several str arguments of the same type, so swapping two of them passes both pyright and the suite.

Approach, in two refactors with a test pair each:
(1) Move the parser out of main() into argument_parser(), so tests parse real argv. Move the composition out of _serve into sites_for(arguments: argparse.Namespace, environment: Mapping[str, str]) -> Sites, a frozen value holding prospect, operator and public_url. It reads INTAKE_* from the mapping it is given, not from os.environ. _serve keeps only the binding, the printing and serve_forever.
(2) Add a frozen Backend descriptor (summary, make_model, banner_html, operator_password_required) and a BACKENDS table keyed by the CLI name. sites_for looks the backend up once; the --backend choices and help come from the table; _model is deleted. A set but empty INTAKE_OPERATOR_PASSWORD counts as unset, for both the start check and the Site. This is the one behaviour change.

Tests go in a new tests/test_serve.py. They drive argument_parser() and sites_for(), and answer requests by calling the composed Sites' public routes directly. No listener is bound; ports 18471 and 18472 appear only as arguments. They assert:
- each site's hosts, with and without INTAKE_PUBLIC_URL;
- the operator's private link is on the public URL;
- the notice page shows the confidentiality notice, not the disclaimer;
- the operator's draft and the released report carry the disclaimer, not the notice (a synthetic full flow);
- the trial banner appears on claude-code and synthetic and never on api;
- api refuses to start without a password, whether it is unset or empty;
- trial backends start without a password;
- a given password guards the operator site on every backend and never the prospect site.

