solar_challenge web/SSE technique (measured 2026-10-11 at main 92d3fe3, werkzeug 3.1.8, Flask 3.1.3, CPython 3.12, task 564 architect). To read the job progress stream (GET /api/jobs/<id>/progress) of a job held running, e.g. by tests/unit/test_web_jobs.py's _BlockingSimulation, one frame at a time in a unit test:
- open it with `with client.get(url, buffered=False) as resp:`, then `frames = resp.iter_encoded()`;
- each next(frames) is one generator yield, i.e. one SSE frame or ':heartbeat';
- werkzeug's run_wsgi_app already pulls the first frame during client.get;
- never call get_data() or list() on a running job's stream: it blocks until the job ends.
On a real threaded werkzeug server (make_server(threaded=True), as `solar-challenge web start` runs it), when the client closes its socket the stream is closed at its next failed heartbeat write: one more get_job_status poll 2.0 s after the close, then none.

