Gotcha (measured, task 7642, vitest 3.2.4): gui vitest with `poolOptions.forks.isolate: false` and multiple forks still builds a FRESH jsdom per test file, while reusing the worker's module cache and Node ESM cache. Three externalized-library captures then go stale after the first file in each worker:
- @testing-library/dom `screen` binds document.body at import;
- @solidjs/testing-library registers afterEach(cleanup) only at import;
- solid-js/web `delegateEvents` in compiled components binds the first file's document, so later clicks never fire.
Fix per file in the setup body: Object.assign(screen, getQueriesForElement(document.body)); delegateEvents([...DelegatedEvents], document); afterEach(cleanup).
vi.mock files also leak via cached importer modules; give them a project with project-level isolate:true. Setup files are re-fetched once per test file even with isolate:false, so fetch-RPC count barely drops (2592 -> 2133); the win is wall time and CPU (~3x).

