Python gotcha for solar_challenge, measured by task 341's architect on 2026-10-03 (base a4bd993; CPython 3.11.15, 3.12.3, 3.13.9, 3.14.4): str(inspect.signature(...)) renders the same source differently on the admitted Python minors.
- 3.11: an Enum's call signature is (value, names=None, *, module=None, ...), against (*values) on 3.12+.
- 3.13+: pathlib.Path renders as pathlib._local.Path.
- 3.14: every evaluated Optional[X] renders as X | None.
The offline lane's interpreter matrix runs every unit test on 3.11, 3.13 and 3.14, so a test that pins raw inspect text passes verify on the 3.12 pin and fails in the lane after merge. Spell annotations canonically instead:
- unions as X | Y;
- classes by bare __qualname__;
- typing aliases by typing.get_origin;
- a ForwardRef by __forward_arg__;
- string annotations verbatim, never evaluated: get_type_hints raises NameError on names imported only under TYPE_CHECKING.
Use Signature.replace with a str subclass whose __repr__ is its text, so inspect still does the layout. This rendered all 69 __all__ names identically on all four minors; task 341 puts it in tests/_surface_forms.py::surface_form.
To run one test file on another minor: UV_PROJECT_ENVIRONMENT=/tmp/<venv> UV_PYTHON=3.X+gil uv run --locked --extra dev pytest <file>. The '+gil' matters: a bare 3.14 picks the free-threaded build on the factory host.

solar_challenge_platform architect gotcha (dark-factory, measured 2026-10-09, task 392). A requeue can leave the task branch as a "chore: save WIP before requeue rebase" commit on an OLD base: the reflog shows "rebase (abort)", because the harness's rebase hit conflicts. When that happens, bring the branch onto main before planning:
- preview the conflicts with `git merge-tree --write-tree main <wip>`;
- run `git rebase main` and resolve each conflicted file to main's version (`git checkout main -- <file>`);
- re-plan those files' edits as pending steps, and pre-satisfy the steps the rebased WIP fully carries with mark_step_committed.
Do NOT `git reset --keep main`. The tip would sit on a main ancestor while this dispatch's branch_base_sha is the old base, so the stranded reconciler's degenerate guard (tip == branch_base_sha) misses, and a restart could MARK_DONE a task with zero work. Do NOT merge main in either. The verify-phase `git rebase main` drops that merge, re-conflicts and aborts, leaving base_commit stale, so the review diff (`git diff <base_commit>...HEAD`) spans all of main since the old base.

