solar_challenge test-helper convention, planned by task 615 (holds once task/615 merges; planned on main 758f36e, 2026-10-10). tests/_plotly_figure.py, pinned by tests/unit/test_plotly_figure_helper.py, is the one home for reading a web.charts builder's Plotly figure JSON in tests.
Its public names:
- sankey_link_values(figure) and sankey_link_colours(figure): each keyed by (source label, target label);
- sankey_node_colours(figure): keyed by label;
- Rgb;
- colour_literals(text): the palette guard's lenient #rrggbb/rgb()/rgba() scanner, yielding (as written, Rgb);
- opaque(colour): one whole colour written as lower-case #rrggbb, alpha dropped.
Every reader raises ValueError rather than guess: on a figure that is not exactly one Sankey trace (including sankey_diagram's "{}"), on a repeated link pair or node label, and on lists of unequal length.
It replaces three private copies: test_web_charts.py::_sankey_links, test_web_chart_energy_flows.py's _RGBA/_opaque and inline readers, and test_web_chart_colours.py's _COLOUR_LITERAL/_colour_literals. A new Sankey or colour-parsing test should import it, not write a copy.

